"""slack-agent: a Slack bot that starts Claude Code sessions from Slack, in Orca workspaces or T3 Code threads.

  slack-agent listen                          run the Socket Mode listener (one per config)

A conversation (<conv>) is a code channel ID (C123) or a session thread (C123-1793.0001).
Helpers the Claude sessions call:
  slack-agent say <conv>                      post stdin (markdown) as the bot
  slack-agent ask <conv> [<option>...]        post stdin and set the session to suspended (waiting for an answer);
                                              each option is a button, and a click comes back as a message
  slack-agent approve <conv> <what>           post Approve/Deny buttons, wait for an owner's click; exit 0 = approved
  slack-agent status <conv> <status>          active | processing | suspended | closed
  slack-agent rename <conv> <title>           rename the session (and the code channel)
  slack-agent step <conv> <id> <status> <title> [<details>]   a live thinking step: pending | in_progress | complete | error;
                                              Slack appends each <details> to the step's earlier ones
  slack-agent open-channel <conv> <title>     move a session thread to a new code channel; prints its ID
  slack-agent finish <conv>                   post stdin as the summary; archive the code channel or close the thread
  slack-agent file <conv> <path> [<comment>]  upload a file
  slack-agent read <conv> [<thread_ts>] [--after <ts>] [--before <ts>] [--limit <n>]
                                              print a channel's or a thread's messages, oldest first
                                              (only channels the config's `channels` allows)
  slack-agent preview <channel>               run the task's app with sign-in; its address and login show in Controls
  slack-agent preview-stop <channel>          stop it
Code channels only:
  slack-agent bar <channel> <key> <label> [<url>] [<icon>]   add or change a context bar item
  slack-agent bar <channel> --remove <key>    remove a context bar item
  slack-agent link <channel> <label> <url> [<note>]   a link people open (a deployment, a page), shown in Controls;
                                              <note> is mrkdwn under it (e.g. the login)
  slack-agent link <channel> --remove <label> remove it
  slack-agent diff <channel> [<base>]         show `git diff <base>` of the cwd as the Code tab
  slack-agent html <channel> <file.html> [<tab name>]   a rendered HTML page as a tab
  slack-agent canvas <channel> <file.md> [<title>]      a Markdown canvas as a tab
  slack-agent tab <channel> --remove <name>   remove a tab you added (by its name or file stem)
  slack-agent plan <channel> <file.md>        create or update the plan canvas (people comment, you edit)
  slack-agent comments <channel>              print the plan canvas and its open comments
App management:
  slack-agent rotate                          renew the app configuration token (it lasts 12 hours)
Used by Claude Code's PreToolUse hook:
  slack-agent gate                            ask for approval before a risky shell command

Extensions (the config's `extensions`) may add commands of their own.

Settings come from the JSON file in $SLACK_AGENT_CONFIG (default ~/.config/slack-agent/config.json);
see config.example.json. Tokens live in the macOS Keychain, service `keychain_service`: bot, app.
On Linux they live in ~/.config/slack-agent/<keychain_service>.json (mode 600), one key per name.
"""

